1️⃣ Project Overview

Seat Booking System is a full-stack web application that allows students to book seats based on batch-wise scheduling rules.

The system ensures:

Controlled seat allocation

Batch-wise access

Time-based restrictions (3 PM rule)

Leave and cancellation support

2️⃣ Tech Stack
Frontend

React.js

Axios (API calls)

LocalStorage (user session)

CSS (custom styling)

Backend

Spring Boot

Spring Data JPA

Hibernate

REST APIs

Maven

Database

MySQL

3️⃣ Database Structure
User Table
Field	Type
id	bigint (PK)
email	varchar
batch	varchar
Booking Table
Field	Type
id	bigint (PK)
date	date
seat_number	int
type	varchar (REGULAR / FLOAT)
is_leave	boolean
user_id	FK
4️⃣ Application Flow
🔹 Step 1: Login

User enters:

Email

Batch (1 or 2)

Backend checks:

If user exists → return user

Else → create new user

User data stored in:

localStorage.setItem("user", JSON.stringify(user));
🔹 Step 2: Dashboard Load

React reads user from localStorage

Calls API:

GET /api/bookings/user/{userId}

Loads:

Seat grid

My Bookings table

🔹 Step 3: Seat Booking Logic
🟢 REGULAR Seats (1–40)

Allowed only on user's scheduled day

🟡 FLOAT Seats (41–50)

Only allowed if:

It is NOT the user's batch day

AND current time is after 3:00 PM

Example Logic:

If Batch 1 day:

Seats 1–40 allowed

Seats 41–50 ❌ not allowed

If not Batch 1 day:

Seats 1–40 ❌ not allowed

Seats 41–50 allowed only after 3 PM

🔹 Step 4: Booking API Call

Frontend sends:

POST /api/bookings
{
  "seatNumber": 12,
  "date": "2026-03-08",
  "type": "REGULAR",
  "isLeave": false,
  "user": { "id": 1 }
}

Backend:

Saves booking

Maps user via foreign key

Stores in MySQL

🔹 Step 5: Leave & Cancel
Leave
PUT /api/bookings/{id}/leave

→ Sets is_leave = true

Cancel
DELETE /api/bookings/{id}

→ Deletes booking record

